-- CAMP-90: a small, real slice of the database for CI.
--
-- 🔴 Why CI needs data at all. Every SEO check added in CAMP-36, 37, 39
-- and 90 inspects the BUILT pages: near-duplicate text, JSON-LD against
-- the schema.org vocabulary, the sitemap against what the pages say,
-- and whether the whole site is closed to indexing. With no database
-- the build produces a site with zero campsites, and every one of those
-- checks either passes vacuously or fails for the wrong reason. A green
-- pipeline that built nothing is worse than a red one.
--
-- Chosen deliberately, not sampled: two regions above the indexing
-- threshold and three below it, at least one campsite with no name, and
-- at least one with a named lake — so every branch the tests exercise
-- exists in the fixture. Picking the first N rows would have made the
-- suite pass while testing half of itself.
--
-- The rows are real OpenStreetMap-derived data, so the same attribution
-- applies here as everywhere: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.
-- Regenerate with: apps/api/test/fixtures/regenerate.sh

